# The release-signing policy and the code that enforces it. This list is the
# release path: a change to any of these files, or to anything under
# .github/workflows/, .github/actions/ or tools/mirror/, needs two counted
# reviewer APPROVEs of its exact head (the `release-path-review` status, Decision 0014). Owners
# here only receive review requests. That status is an accident guard, not a
# security boundary. scripts/check_release_policy.py (the required
# `release-policy` check) keeps this list complete.
# The Pulp-to-Vellum framework transfer is judged by verify_extraction.py
# and framework_trusted_verify.py against the transfer record, the name-debt
# baseline and the external-updates log under provenance/; the record files
# are owned before they exist so the change that adds them needs both reviews.
# provenance/framework/ports.json is left out on purpose: the ledger is data
# those judges check row by row, so a port lands by normal review.
